-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §63 (part יד, הרחבת הוראות ההסכם): the
-- organisation applies to the Minister of Industry, Trade and Labour for an
-- extension order extending the agreement, under §25 of the Collective
-- Agreements Law, to further employers of teaching employees in the upper
-- divisions.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`
IMPORT collective_agreements_law

§ `63`

DECLARE `Oz section 63 action` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Minister for an extension order extending the agreement`

-- ¶1: the parties agree that the organisation applies; no day is set
-- (convention dates.no-deadline). Whether the Minister extends it is his,
-- under §25 of the Collective Agreements Law, 1957 (l4/laws/).
@ref akn:art_63/p1
`applying for an extension order` MEANS
    PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
    MUST  `apply to the Minister for an extension order extending the agreement`

-- §25 lets the Minister extend only a general collective agreement, and
-- only where he thinks it right by the number of employees and employers
-- it applies to and its weight in labour relations. Which kind this
-- agreement is, §63 does not say: the kind is an input here, and what the
-- organisation's application can bring about turns on it.
@ref akn:art_63/p1
GIVEN k IS A `kind of collective agreement`, `the Minister thinks it right, by the section's measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application under Oz §63 can bring an extension order` k `the Minister thinks it right, by the section's measures` IF
    `the Minister may extend it under section 25` k `the Minister thinks it right, by the section's measures`

#ASSERT `the application under Oz §63 can bring an extension order` `a general collective agreement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the application under Oz §63 can bring an extension order` `a general collective agreement` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the application under Oz §63 can bring an extension order` `a special collective agreement` TRUE
